{"id":310,"slug":"the-discreet-charm-of-the-bourgeoisie","title":"The Discreet Charm of the Bourgeoisie","year":1972,"country":"France","duration":101,"spine":102,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/310-the-discreet-charm-of-the-bourgeoisie","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/ec5399163d6dca9c04ee961a15f1c863/JegycjW6BfTUczUHnh51sLyJCVKQoy_large.jpg","description":"In Luis Buñuel’s deliciously satiric masterpiece, an upper-middle-class sextet sits down to a dinner that is continually delayed, their attempts to eat thwarted by vaudevillian events both actual and imagined, including terrorist attacks, military maneuvers, and ghostly apparitions. Stringing together a discontinuous, digressive series of absurdist set pieces, Buñuel and his screenwriting partner Jean-Claude Carrière send a cast of European-film greats—including Fernando Rey, Stéphane Audran, Delphine Seyrig, Jean-Pierre Cassel, and Bulle Ogier—through a maze of desire deferred, frustrated, and interrupted. The Oscar-winning pinnacle of Buñuel’s late-career ascent as a feted maestro of the international art house, The Discreet Charm of the Bourgeoisie is also one of his most gleefully radical assaults on the values of the ruling class.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Luis Buñuel","slug":"luis-bunuel"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Fernando Rey","role":"Rafael Acosta, the ambassador","slug":"fernando-rey"},{"actor":"Paul Frankeur","role":"François Thévenot","slug":"paul-frankeur"},{"actor":"Delphine Seyrig","role":"Simone Thévenot","slug":"delphine-seyrig"},{"actor":"Bulle Ogier","role":"Florence, her sister","slug":"bulle-ogier"},{"actor":"Stéphane Audran","role":"Alice Sénéchal","slug":"stephane-audran"},{"actor":"Jean-Pierre Cassel","role":"Henri Sénéchal","slug":"jean-pierre-cassel"},{"actor":"Julien Bertheau","role":"Monsignor Dufour","slug":"julien-bertheau"},{"actor":"Milena Vukotic","role":"Inès, the maid","slug":"milena-vukotic"},{"actor":"Maria Gabriella Maione","ro